From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 11:32:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] mb/lenovo/m720q_m920q: An ACPI node for the M.2 Wi-Fi card

At every boot Linux prints "ACPI: \: failed to evaluate _DSM
2c176672-0b22-294b-814f-75e4dd26b5fd" twice: iwlwifi asks the product
reset _DSM (7266172C-220B-4B29-814F-75E4DD26B5FD) of the ACPI node of
the card, which has none, and the NULL handle fails with
AE_BAD_PARAMETER. Declare the card, _ADR 0, with no methods: a missing
_DSM is AE_NOT_FOUND, which acpi_evaluate_dsm() does not report. No
_PRW, as before: the wake of the card stays the OS's.

The card is behind root port 6, the only port on of 00:1c, which the
PCH then puts at function 0: lspci lists it as 00:1c.0, and Linux gives
it the node with _ADR 0x001c0000, RP01, not RP06. The node goes there.

TEST=On an M920x, a first version under RP06 was in the DSDT and Linux
still warned: 00:1c.0 has the firmware node \_SB_.PCI0.RP01.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/dsdt.asl | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/dsdt.asl b/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/dsdt.asl
index 777df2d431..cc071dcad9 100644
--- a/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/dsdt.asl
+++ b/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/dsdt.asl
@@ -21,6 +21,21 @@ DefinitionBlock(
 		#include <soc/intel/cannonlake/acpi/southbridge.asl>
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * The M.2 Wi-Fi card behind root port 6, with no method: iwlwifi asks
+	 * its _DSM for the product reset and, without an ACPI node for the card,
+	 * warns at every boot (AE_BAD_PARAMETER); a missing method is quiet.
+	 * Port 6 is the only one on of 00:1c, which the PCH then puts at
+	 * function 0: the OS gives it the node with _ADR 0x001c0000, RP01.
+	 */
+	Scope (\_SB.PCI0.RP01)
+	{
+		Device (WIFI)
+		{
+			Name (_ADR, 0)
+		}
+	}
+
 	/* What macOS looks for on this desktop, under macOS only */
 	#include "acpi/macos.asl"
 
